  "summary": "Kyle Green is a dynamic force in the world of martial arts, media, and modern storytelling. A dedicated practitioner of traditional Kung Fu, Kyle Green trains at the esteemed Trinity Training Center in Peoria, Illinois (peoriakungfu.com) under the tutelage of Sigung Dexter Parker, where discipline, philosophy, and skill converge on the path of mastery. \n\n\nIn addition to his martial training, Kyle Green is a writer and representative for Action Martial Arts Magazine and Action Martial Arts Magazine TV, where he contributes to elevating voices and stories from across the global martial arts community. \n\n\nHe currently serves as the Technical Director and TYGA Kung Fu Representative for TYGA Martial Arts International (USA), an organization dedicated to preserving and promoting authentic martial traditions with modern impact.\n\n\nAs an ambassador and one of two official publicists of the Sport Karate Museum, an official Ambassador of the Universal Martial Arts Hall of Fame. Kyle Green plays an active role in honoring the legacy and evolution of martial arts pioneers, bridging generations of warriors and champions.\n\n\nExpanding his influence into film and digital media, Kyle Green is also the Head Web Designer and Full-Service Film Publicist and Content Producer for SOCA Entertainment, the innovative media company founded by Brian \"Tightest\" Yarbrough and Sifu Ed \"Eddy P\" Parker. \n\n\nHis creative work supports a wide range of projects—from films to cultural events/seminars and martial arts organizations.\n\n\nHe is the published author of The Way of the Modern Warrior: The Bushido Code of the Modern Era available now on Amazon in eBook and paperback!\n\n\nWhether on the training floor, on the web, or through the written word, Kyle Green embodies the mindset of a Modern Warrior—committed to excellence, authenticity, and legacy.",
